They _can_ wear armor.  They can't cast spells well in it, but early
on it's sometimes worth machine-gunning daggers, letting the pet
fight, spamming Elbereth, and wearing armor.  Once you find all the
ancillary armor (gloves, hat, shoes, small shield) and studded
leather, you can go to non-metal body armor (especially if you manage
to find a piece at +2 and other at +1, or something like that).  In
the interim, wear that mithril proudly.

The basics are the same as most low-level characters: Kill things at
range (wizards can get expert dagger, meaning "machine gun").  Run
away and use your pets.  Stick with that staff for melee early, until
you've at least gotten skilled dagger (unless you find/ID an enchanted
dagger or something else really nice)--but avoid melee.  Elbereth.
Buy protection when possible.

Make use of what the game gives you--reasonable chance of a wish in
minetown, or once you can handle a water demon #dip fountains up to
the Oracle level trying for one.  Co-aligned or unattended altars are
a huge boon.  SDSM is really nice.  Magicbane is really nice.

You start with a lot of inventory--figure out the best way to use each
item and maximize its value.



